      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most common attack against UBI is the potential for a massive disincentive to work, leading to a decline in the labor force and a resulting economic contraction. Another strong criticism is the immense, potentially unsupportable, cost and the necessary tax burden required to fund it. A powerful rebuttal to the \"unworkable\" claim is to argue that UBI can support smaller, more flexible side-gigs, and the \"unsupportable cost\" argument must be balanced against the massive societal savings from reduced poverty and healthcare needs.",
